# Design System Rail

Portable constraint: the model must not invent color or layout freely — only select from the pre-engineered rail of tokens, shared primitives, and named layout archetypes. Treat as an engineering constraint, not a suggestion.

## ScanLogic adaptation (filled blanks)

| Blank | Value |
|-------|--------|
| Framework / UI kit | React 19 + Vite 8 + Tailwind 4; shared shell via `AppShell`, `premium-card`, module patterns — prefer existing primitives over new libraries |
| Design input | One primary brand hue (or short vibe). Derive secondary/muted/accent/surfaces from it. Do not interview for a full palette. |
| Layout archetypes | `suite-shell`, `module-home`, `wizard-steps`, `ai-chat-immersive`, `centered-form`, `settings-stack` |
| Extra semantic tokens | `brand-*`, `surface` / `surface-elevated` / `surface-card`, success/warning/destructive when needed — add in `src/index.css` `@theme` first |

Canonical token file: `src/index.css` (`@theme` + `:root`).

## Cursor enforcement

Whenever a task involves UI (pages, components, forms, tables, dashboards, auth, landing, settings, mobile/responsive, dark surfaces, admin), apply this rail automatically.

Before creating UI:

1. Search the codebase for reusable components.
2. Prefer composition over duplication.
3. Never create a second implementation of an existing component.
4. Extend existing primitives whenever possible.

